    m_Alignment: 3
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1.5
  m_Text: "When the ball is launched, its initial velocity can be separated into
    horizontal and vertical components. The horizontal velocity remains constant
    because horizontal acceleration is assumed to be zero. Meanwhile, gravity continuously
    accelerates the ball downward at 9.81 m/s\xB2, causing its vertical velocity
    to change. Together, these two motions create the ball's curved, parabolic trajectory."
